PXE_PREPARE=(archlinux ubuntu debian rocky fedora freebsd netbsd clonezilla gparted memtest)
PXE_MENUS=(
    "-Distros" archlinux ubuntu debian rocky fedora freebsd netbsd
    "-Utilities" clonezilla gparted tool reboot)

PXE_LOCAL_ROOT=/srv/pxe
PXE_HTTP_ROOT=http://10.123.123.1/pxe
PXE_NFS_HOST=10.123.123.1
PXE_NFS_ROOT=/srv/pxe

# Operator-provided big assets (ISOs, netboot tarballs). Scripts use files found
# here and only download when missing. Default: <dirname of PXE_LOCAL_ROOT>/downloads.
#   freebsd/<ver>/FreeBSD-<ver>-RELEASE-amd64-disc1.iso + CHECKSUM.SHA256-FreeBSD-<ver>-RELEASE-amd64
#   debian/<stable|testing>/netboot.tar.gz + SHA256SUMS
#PXE_DOWNLOADS=/srv/pxe-downloads
# FreeBSD releases to serve; unset = every freebsd/<ver>/ dir in PXE_DOWNLOADS that has a disc1.iso.
#FREEBSD_VERSIONS="14.5 15.1"
# iPXE first stage binaries (undionly.kpxe, snponly.efi); default: <PXE_DOWNLOADS>/ipxe, then /usr/lib/ipxe.
#PXE_IPXE_DIR=/srv/pxe-downloads/ipxe
#FREEBSD_ARCHES="amd64"
# Debian local netboot cache: auto (use local tarballs), fetch (also download missing), off.
#DEBIAN_NETBOOT_CACHE=auto
#DEBIAN_NETBOOT_SUITES="stable testing"

PXE_TITLE="USTC Network Boot Service (http://pxe.ustc.edu.cn/)"
PXE_INTRO="
== USTC Network Boot Service ==

Website: http://pxe.ustc.edu.cn/

This is the USTC Network Boot Service provided by:
- Linux User Group (https://lug.ustc.edu.cn/)
- Network and Information Center (https://ustcnet.ustc.edu.cn/)
- Library (https://lib.ustc.edu.cn)

If you get here by mistake, please reboot, check the BIOS/UEFI firmware
settings and disable network boot.

If you need help, please contact lug@ustc.edu.cn."
